FFmpeg — LGPL-2.1-or-later
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
This software links against FFmpeg (avformat, avcodec, avutil, swresample)
and is not itself a work of FFmpeg. FFmpeg is used under the LGPL only: no
build produced by this repository may be configured with --enable-gpl or
--enable-nonfree, and the generated config.h must report CONFIG_GPL 0.

Full license text: https://www.gnu.org/licenses/old-licenses/lgpl-2.1.html
Source: https://ffmpeg.org/download.html

The obligation differs by platform, and both halves are met here:

  Desktop (macOS, Linux, Windows). FFmpeg remains a set of separate,
  dynamically linked libraries that an end user can replace with their own
  build. native/windows/build.ps1 downloads a pinned LGPL binary
  distribution; native/macos/build.sh and native/linux/build.sh link against
  whatever LGPL-only FFmpeg pkg-config is pointed at.

  Mobile (iOS, Android). FFmpeg is linked statically into the façade, because
  a phone has no package manager to obtain one from. Replaceability is
  therefore met by relink route rather than by dynamic linking:
  native/ios/build-ffmpeg.sh and native/android/build-ffmpeg.sh contain the
  exact FFmpeg version and the exact configure line used, and rebuilding the
  binary from an FFmpeg of the user's own choosing is those two scripts plus
  the corresponding build.sh.

Anyone distributing a binary built from this repository is responsible for
carrying that source offer onward.
